ed_atlas_row","component_id":"world_model_projection_drift_control_room","ref_kind":"principle","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[world_model_projection_drift_control_room].principle_refs"}],"cited_by_count":41,"component_ids":["annex_knowledge_routing","bounded_autonomy_campaign_packet","bridge_campaign_dag_validation","bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","certificate_kernel_execution_lab","cognitive_operator_registry","cold_reader_route_map","derived_fact_provider_runtime","egress_self_compliance_audit","engine_room_demo","finite_erdos_denominator_certificate_strike","formal_evidence_cell_anchor_resolver","formal_math_lean_proof_witness","formal_math_premise_retrieval","formal_math_readiness_gate","formal_math_verifier_trace_repair_loop","generated_projection_drift_runtime","lean_proof_search_lab_runtime","lean_std_premise_index","materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay","mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer","mechanistic_interpretability_circuit_attribution_replay","metabolism_queue_reconciliation","navigation_fitness_benchmark","navigation_hologram_route_plane","pattern_assimilation_step","pattern_binding_contract","proof_diagnostic_evidence_spine","provider_context_recipe_budget_policy","public_reveal_walkthrough","research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","ring2_premise_retrieval_precision_recall_harness","routing_anti_patterns_registry","semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","spatial_world_model_counterfactual_simulation_replay","tactic_portfolio_availability_probe","target_shape_tactic_routing_gate","undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier","verifier_lab_execution_spine","verifier_lab_kernel","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":[],"id":"P-3","kind":"principle","plain":"Let a small verifier, parser, harness, compiler route, registry contract or kernel decide what is trusted, in place of a broad written account of why a result looks right. The code that produces results may be large; the code that decides should be small enough for a person to read and rerun.","principles":[],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The weighing plate covers only who decides and why the shopper is kept out; a simple checker can still make mistakes of its own.","maps":[{"analogy":"the weighing plate that checks each item again","doctrine":"the small checker that rereads and decides"},{"analogy":"the shopper, who cannot confirm their own bag","doctrine":"the large producer kept out of the decision"}],"text":"At a self-checkout, the weighing plate weighs each item again to confirm what was scanned. The shopper packing the bag never gets to declare the bag correct."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A large model is trusted because it sounds sure of its answer, and no separate checker rereads anything, so the producer is also the judge.","does_not_prove":"A small checker is easier to audit, and it can still be wrong.","enforced_in_component_ids":["certificate_kernel_execution_lab","formal_math_lean_proof_witness","verifier_lab_kernel"],"example":{"component_ids":["certificate_kernel_execution_lab"],"text":"The certificate kernel lab keeps producers and the checker apart. A producer writes certificate material and a small kernel rereads it and decides, so the deciding code is the part you can read and rerun."},"governs":"Where trust sits, between a large producer and the small checker that decides.","plain":"Put your trust in one small, simple step that redoes the work and decides. The large, complicated program that produced the answer stays out of that decision, because the thing being judged should not judge itself.","potential_misread":"That a capable, confident producer can vouch for its own output, when once the producer decides, no independent check is left.","refuses":"Accepting a large producer's own confidence in place of a small check that someone can read and rerun.","requires":"A small checker that rereads a certificate and accepts or rejects it, with the producer outside the decision.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"The part you have to audit and rerun stays small, even when the systems producing answers grow large and hard to inspect."},"rests_on":["AX-2"],"source_ref":"PRINCIPLES.md::P-3","statement":"Grounding: AX-2.\nObligation grounding: AX-2.O1.small_checker_decides, AX-2.O2.producer_emits_certificate, AX-2.O3.invalid_proof_rejected.\n\nLet a small verifier, parser, harness, compiler route, registry contract or\nkernel decide what is trusted, in place of a broad written account of why a\nresult looks right. The code that produces results may be large; the code that\ndecides should be small enough for a person to read and rerun.","statement_sha256":"0e56cd97efada9bc24525b2a85bea45836a3705107c300ca0e1f49fed9be8b1f","title":"Concentrate trust in small checkers","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}